 not installed. If you'd rather have the stable line, that is Prisma 7.10.1 with `@prisma/client`, which would be a different setup.\n- **Schema:** `User` (unique `email`, optional `name`) and `Post` (`title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to false, one author). I dropped the scaffold's extra example fields.\n- **Database:** I previewed with `--dry-run`, then created the tables. I confirmed them with `psql`, and the rows match what the script printed.\n- **Script:** each run creates a user with a timestamp in the email, so it can be re-run without a unique-constraint error.\n- **Other changes:** the scaffold also changed `package.json`, `tsconfig.json` (`module` to `preserve`, `types: [\"node\"]`), and `.gitignore`. `src/index.ts` and `.env` are untouched.\n- **Not done:** nothing is committed, and I did not run `npx prisma skills sync`, which the CLI suggested.\n\nANSWER.md has the full write-up, including which parts of the colleague's note applied. The checks I relied on were the dist-tags, the `--dry-run` output, `tsc --noEmit`, the script run, and the `psql` queries. The note's warning about an rc `contract emit` crash did not reproduce on rc.33.","ttft_ms":2422,"type":"result","duration_ms":98431,"uuid":"d9ac3230-4bff-4d3b-98fa-ec1aa08143ca","ttft_stream_ms":1682,"time_to_request_ms":358,"first_content_frame_ms":1682,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":9715,"cacheReadInputTokens":370181,"cacheCreationInputTokens":25538,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.01366931,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3844,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":25538,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T22:27:53.640Z"}
